    "method": "electron",
    "beam": "Backward negative muons of about 87 MeV/c (before the degrader), up to 1000 per second, 100 % duty cycle. Electrons and remaining pions rejected by pulse height in a beam counter.",
    "target": "Mostly elemental, self-supporting targets; some powders, liquids and compounds (fluorides, oxides, CCl4 ...) in thin stainless-steel or plastic containers; liquid nitrogen in an insulated container. Impurities below 1 %. Muons stopping in the scintillators give a carbon component (1-2 % of the stops), fixed for light elements with runs on a brass plate of equal stopping power.",
    "detector": "Plastic scintillation counters: beam counters behind a 2.5 cm lead collimator, a veto counter, and electron counters (one cylindrical counter and four paddles) covering about 60 % of 4 pi."
